course: dictionary
lesson: 269
title: Strange things from the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. Ambergris is one of them. Context clues can help you work out what it is. «Ambergris is a waxy lump that forms in a sperm whale's gut.» Waxy and lump tell you it is solid and a bit like candle wax, and gut tells you it is inside a whale.
explain: The sentence also tells you that it can «wash ashore». Ashore means onto the land, so ambergris is something the sea carries to the beach. Put the clues together and you can say ambergris is a waxy grey material from whales that can float on the sea.
explain: Clues can also tell a story about how people used a thing. «It was used in perfume for hundreds of years.» Hundreds of years means a very long time, so people valued ambergris for a long time. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: Ambergris is a waxy, grey substance made in the gut of sperm whales.
fact: It is sometimes found floating in the sea or washed up on beaches.
fact: Long ago, people used ambergris in perfumes, and it was traded like treasure.
fact: Ambergris is uncountable, so you say a lump of ambergris, not two ambergrises.
fact: Some countries now ban selling it, which means they have made a rule against it.
exercise: «Ambergris is a waxy lump that forms in a sperm whale's gut.» What is ambergris made in? | A lump of salt | *A sperm whale's gut | A rock on the beach | A squid's shell
exercise: «Ambergris can wash ashore.» What does ashore mean? | Far away in space | *Onto the land from the sea | Deep in a cave | Under the ice
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that tells you what ambergris feels like. | *waxy | whale | squid | beaks
test: «It was used in perfume for hundreds of years.» What does hundreds of years tell you? | *It was used for a very long time | It was used only for one day | It was used only by whales | It was never used at all
test: Which phrase is correct for ambergris? | *a lump of ambergris | an ambergris | two ambergrises | many ambergrises
exam: «Some countries now ban selling it.» What does ban mean here? | Sell it very cheaply | Hide it under the sand | *Officially forbid | Paint it bright red
